# Slice 289 (INDEX-NUMERIC-RECEPTION): a write through the L3 INDEX of a machine pointer an own field holds, with an int index,
# in a program without the receiver of the conversion: CHECK admits the index by the ordinary numeric reception before the
# value, as the walker's ELEMPUT selects the place first -- so the index's refusal comes before the value's.
[]: int cells 2
@: pc int @ cells[0U]
int: at 1
pc[at]: "text"
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: cells[1U]; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
